{
  "//": [
    "A STARTING permission set for a new Claude Code instance on this project.",
    "",
    "Copy to the PARENT of the repo checkout as .claude/settings.local.json - the",
    "session's working directory is the parent (C:/.../Projects), not the repo, which is",
    "also why the repo's CLAUDE.md does not auto-load and must be read deliberately.",
    "",
    "This is a curated replacement, NOT a copy: the machine it came from had accumulated",
    "803 allow entries, 233 of them one-off literal ssh commands, because each prompt was",
    "answered individually over weeks. Generalized patterns do the same work without",
    "re-prompting. Everything here is read/build/deploy work this project does constantly.",
    "",
    "Deliberately NOT granted, so they stay a decision: force-push, rm -rf, docker/compose",
    "run directly against the host, and anything that writes secrets. Ships and releases",
    "(gh release create/delete, Ship.ps1) are also left to prompt - they are outward-facing."
  ],
